# esx-announce

Read devel-loop/communication.md and esx/project.json. The configured channel and
format are routing preferences; the current owner's authorization controls sending.
Write and validate the underlying project record before announcing its result.

Use the available authorized provider tool. Include the issue ID, scientific/user
consequence and honest status in roughly 80 words; keep under 200. Avoid tables,
large code blocks and internal hashes. Link the detailed project record when an
accessible link exists. Save the actual returned receipt/link or a concrete delivery
explanation. After a delivery change, refresh closeout history using --check-done.
The skill never treats a configured channel as permission or a fabricated timestamp
as evidence. A failed/unavailable post does not block scientific work.
